-- A rule that reads a section binder takes it as an extra input, which a bare
-- mention of the rule's name cannot carry. Passing such a rule as a value is a
-- check error naming it; the way to write it is a lambda that applies it,
-- `map (GIVEN x YIELD bump x) …`, which ok/section-given-discharge.l4 shows.

IMPORT prelude

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN `the rate` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
bump n MEANS n TIMES `the rate`

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`all bumped` MEANS map bump (LIST 1, 2, 3)
